==Culture==
{{See also|Society of Balisca}}
Navassa and its hinterland have a culture that is distinct from the rest of Balisca, and is commonly seen as more closely related to that of the [[Community of Volisania]] (specifically the [[Volisan Countries]]), rather to Balisca itself. Hence, these areas are collectively known as "''Nova'' ''Volisanii''", after the [[w:Hispania Tarraconensis|Mesogean name for the Mormac tribe]] of the Western Illypnia. This region, and in particular Navassa, has played an important role as a center of early Baliscan culture since the 17th century, first in Abyala, and from the 19th century on, worldwide. The city's founders, consisting of a mix of [[w:Moriscos|Moriscos]], [[Bayani Baliscans|Bayanis]], [[Imfezzan Baliscans|Imfezzans]], [[w:Romani people|Romani]], [[Catharism|Cathars]], Catholics and Muslims reflected the diversity of the Mesogean colonial effort and left a lasting legacy on the city. 

Navassa emerged as one of the most-prominent Volisanian-speaking cities during the years of the Volisan Empire, spreading Volisanian culture around [[Lurando-Abyala]]. Today, Navassa continues this role as a center of Volisanian culture in Balisca, but is increasingly overshadowed by cities such as [[Merced]]. There are also a number of well-preserved traditional Catharist festivities throughout the year. [[W:Holy Week|Holy Week]] celebrations in Navassa are considered some of the most colorful in Balisca. Additionally, celebration of [[w:Saint George's Day (Spain)|Saint George's Day]] is shared between Navassa and Volisania (specifically the former territories of the [[United Kingdoms of Volisania|United Kingdoms]]), however, yellow roses are more commonly associated with Navassan celebrations, rather than the red roses typically seen in other countries. 

The city received significant waves of Volisan refugees who were fleeing the chaos of the [[W:French Revolutionary Wars|French Revolutionary Wars]]. Immigration and urbanization in the nineteenth and twentieth centuries have also created new socioeconomic communities, both urban (like Eix, Empuria, Sant Martí, and Cituat Nova) and the suburban and working class hinterlands (like Banyoles) of the urban agglomeration (called variously ''afores'' ("suburbs", sometimes qualified as "chic" or "pobre" or ''els finques'' "housing projects") which have developed their own "sense of place" and local culture (such as [[Fila Carpa]]; "tent city"), as well as cultural identity.

In addition to Volisanian (the official language of Estuaria), [[Estuarian Creole|Créyòl]] is widely spoken, and is the co-official language of the entirety of the Metropolitan City, according to the city's [[Gran Carta]]. Prior to 1921, Navassa officially labelled itself "unilingual", only recognizing Standard Estuarian Volisanian as an official language. The institution that governs Estuarian Creole, the [[Acadèmia Créyòl de la Llengua]] (ACL), is headquartered in Navassa. The concentration of Créyòl speakers in Navassa reflects the city's roots as the home of the Tarracos (also called ''Pantans volisanians''; "swamp Volisanians").

The characteristic Volisania of this city is ''Napitxat'', a dialect of the metropolitan area of ​​Navassa. Despite being highly influenced by Standard Volisanian, ''Napitxat'' retains certain ancient characteristics that have been lost in the rest of the Estuarian dialects. Its main characteristics are:

*Deafening of the voiced alveolars and palatals , as at home , tretze and metge ['kasa,' tretse, 'metxe] (home, thirteen and doctor, respectively).
*The one that conserves archaic forms of the plural, which maintain the original Latin n , as in hòmens [homes] (men) or jóvens [joves] (young people).
*The one that has a certain tendency to diphthongization of the unstressed initial o (when it is constituted in a syllable) by au: aulor [smell] (smell), aufegar [offegar] (to drown), aubrir [obrir] (to open).

===Architecture===
{{Main|Architecture of Balisca}}

{{multiple image
| direction         = vertical
| align             = left
| width1            = 250
| width2            = 250
| footer            = 
| image1            = Palau Céspedes.jpg
| caption1          = [[Palau Céspedes]], in the [[Eixample]] district. It is currently home to the the flagship [[Basileus]] hotel
| image2            = Navassa canal ivy.png
