==Government and politics==
{{Main|Communal politics in Balisca}}

[[File:Navassa government quarter.png|thumb|[[Navassa Cabildo]], the seat of the [[Ajuntament de Navaza]], is located in the [[Jiròni, Navassa|Jiròni]] district of the city]]
Navassa's administration is handled by a {{W|municipal council|communal council}}, the [[Ajuntament de Navaza]], which is consists of 15 councillors. The councils are directly elected for a four-year terms by universal suffrage. 

Navassa is subject to a special law articulated through the [[Gran Carta]] (Communal compact). The first version of this compact was adopted in 1860 and has since been amended numerous times, with the current version having been approved in June 2021. According to this compact, Navassa's council is organised in two levels: a cooperative one, with elected city councillors, and one political which overseas the programs and executes the decisions taken on the cooperative level. 

===Public safety===
The [[Civil Guard (Navassa)|Guàrdia Civil]] (Civil Guard) is the local public safety body serving Navassa, and is accountable to direct civil oversight. As of 2018, it had a workforce of 6,190 civil servants. Members of the Municipal Guard are prohibited from carrying lethal weapons. Additionally, in response to the widespread protests during the [[2021 Baliscan civil unrest|2021 civil unrest]], the ''Ajuntament'' banned the usage of {{W|tear gas}} and {{W|rubber bullets}} as a deterrent to protests.

The headquarters of both the Directorate-General of Public Safety and the Directorate-General of the [[Confederal Militia]] are located in Eixample. The headquarters of the Higher Office of Public Safetty of Navassa (Oficina Superior de Policia de Navaza), the cantonal [[Autonomous Militia]] with jurisdiction over the region also lies in Eixample. Potential abuse committed by city's public safety are monitored by the communally organized watchdog ''Projecte de carrers pacífics'' ("Peaceful Streets Project"), which provides reports to the Ajuntament monthly. Additionally, the Ajuntament restricts the Civil Guard's budget increases to a maximum of two percent per year. 

Crime rates vary widely across different areas of Navassa. Crime figures are made available nationally at communal and cantonal-level. In 2024, there were 11 homicides, a 8.3% decrease over 2023. The Civil Guard is required to make detailed crime figures, broken down by category at communal and cantonal level, readily available on their website since 2000. Recorded [[W:Violent crime|violent crime]] has been falling in Navassa steadily since the 1990s, while nonviolent crime such as [[W:Pickpocketing|pickpocketing]], [[W:Shoplifting|shoplifting]] and motor vehicle theft have risen.
==Geography and climate==
{{Main|Balisca#Geography}}

Navassa has a [[w:Humid subtropical climate|humid subtropical climate]] (''Cfa'', according to the [[w:Köppen climate classification|Köppen climate classification]]). The city has cool Winters (June to September), warm-hot Summers (December to March) and volatile Springs (October and November); there are numerous [[W:Thunderstorm|thunderstorms]] but no tropical cyclones. Rainfall is regular and evenly spread throughout the year, reaching around {{convert|950|mm|in}}.

Winters are generally cool, wet, windy and overcast. During this season, there are bursts of icy and relatively dry winds of continental polar air masses, giving an unpleasant chilly feeling to the everyday life of the city. Frosts occur few times during winter, generally not falling below 28° F (-2° C) because of the oceanic influence that moderates the temperature; few miles away from the coast, frosts are more common and colder. Rainfall and [[Ice pellets|sleet]] are a infrequent winter occurrence, but snowfall is almost non-existent. 

Summers are warm-hot and humid, with less wind than other seasons. During this season, a moderate wind often blows from the sea in the evenings which has a pleasant cooling effect on the city, in contrast to the more severe summer heat of nearby cities like [[Bixessarri]]. Heat waves come with the north winds, which bring humid and hot air masses from the tropical interior of the South American continent. These warm periods are usually followed by thunderstorms, generated by cold fronts of the southwest that lowers temperatures considerably. This phenomenon is regional, and can occur several times all year long.


